    "time_horizon": "long-term",
    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "This policy primarily affects a very small number of people seeking legal gender recognition, so its direct impact on population-wide social trust and community cohesion is likely minimal. The evidence provided focuses on individual dignity and legal process rather than community-level belonging or civic participation.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether legal recognition of non-binary identities shifts broader social attitudes and inter-group relations at population scale \u2014 evidence on that causal link is absent from the provided sources.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "tier": "stated",
        "claim": "The policy would remove medical report requirements, recognise non-binary identities in law, and remove the spousal veto from the gender recognition process.",
