      "notes": "The verdict is internally consistent and well-disciplined. All claims are correctly tiered; the E17 ONS figure is treated as measurable with appropriate caveats noted elsewhere in the evidence set (E18/E19 flagging ONS reclassification \u2014 the verdict does not over-rely on the figure, using it only to bound population size which is directionally robust regardless). The E13 advocacy claim is correctly labelled projected. Direction 'negligible' with magnitude 'minor' is slightly inconsistent (minor implies some measurable effect; negligible implies effectively none) but not a blocking issue \u2014 the rationale makes the intended meaning clear (positive within-group, undetectable at population scale). No lever leakage: the verdict correctly judges effect on O15 indicators rather than scoring GRC reform as a policy goal. No party-blind violations. No false balance: the verdict reaches negligible rather than mixed, consistent with the absence of population-scale O15 evidence. The biggest_unknown is genuine and well-stated."
